WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.029 --> 00:00:02.931
- [Woman] This is a California roll,

00:00:02.931 --> 00:00:04.975
and it was probably invented in Japan.

00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:05.861
- [Man] Wrong.

00:00:05.861 --> 00:00:07.084
- [Woman] Oh, California?

00:00:07.084 --> 00:00:10.782
- [Man] Nope, it was invented in Canada.

00:00:10.782 --> 00:00:12.304
- [Woman] Oh.

00:00:12.304 --> 00:00:13.804
This is Chef Tojo.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.638
- [Woman] He helped make
sushi one of the most popular

00:00:17.638 --> 00:00:19.479
foods in the U.S. and Canada.

00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:22.780
- [Man] But to understand this,
we have to take a look back.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.409
It was 1971, and sushi wasn't popular.

00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:27.681
When it came to Japanese food,

00:00:27.681 --> 00:00:30.514
people only liked a couple things.

00:00:33.131 --> 00:00:34.895
- [Woman] Turns out, North Americans,

00:00:34.895 --> 00:00:37.062
they did not like seaweed.

00:00:41.715 --> 00:00:43.947
- [Woman] So Tojo did something crazy.

00:00:43.947 --> 00:00:46.677
- [Man] He wrapped the rice
on the outside of the seaweed.

00:00:46.677 --> 00:00:48.427
- [Woman] To hide it.

00:00:56.265 --> 00:01:00.182
- [Woman] And Chef Tojo,
he did not stop there.

00:01:08.851 --> 00:01:11.534
- [Man] So he rolled these
preferred ingredients into one--

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:12.367
- [Woman] Beautiful.

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:13.200
- [Man] Amazing.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.533
- [Man And Woman] Cuisine-changing roll.

00:01:19.538 --> 00:01:21.524
- [Woman] Word is, it got
the name California Roll,

00:01:21.524 --> 00:01:23.044
because it was so popular with people

00:01:23.044 --> 00:01:26.633
who came to his restaurant from L.A.

00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:27.762
- [Man] And the roll made people think

00:01:27.762 --> 00:01:29.164
differently about sushi.

00:01:29.164 --> 00:01:32.747
- [Woman] It was some
sort of gateway roll.

00:01:40.894 --> 00:01:44.185
- [Woman] Chef Tojo's beginner
roll was such a success,

00:01:44.185 --> 00:01:46.705
Japan's Ministry of Agriculture,
Forestry, and Fisheries

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:49.404
appointed him as the
nation's Goodwill Ambassador

00:01:49.404 --> 00:01:50.836
for Japanese cuisine.

00:01:50.836 --> 00:01:53.025
- [Man] And now, sushi is everywhere.

00:01:53.025 --> 00:01:54.294
Stickers on your notebook.

00:01:54.294 --> 00:01:55.522
- [Woman] USB drives.

00:01:55.522 --> 00:01:56.624
- [Man] Play-Doh molds.

00:01:56.624 --> 00:01:58.731
- [Woman] Wooden toy sets everywhere.

00:01:58.731 --> 00:02:00.699
- [Man] Maybe not all
thanks to Chef Tojo--

00:02:00.699 --> 00:02:02.648
- [Woman] But definitely partly.

00:02:02.648 --> 00:02:06.315
(soft, bouncy doo wop song)

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.207
(chiming)

